{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775342461-pxCctNl2BnKM2eW2Uasl","role":"assistant","created":1775342465,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Treasury Bulletin document doesn't contain historical saving rate data from 1950-1990 - it only has data up to 1991 (through first half). It mentions that the long-term average is 6.7%, but doesn't give historical data for 1950-1990.\n\nLet me search more extensively in this document for any historical data, or maybe there's more specific data in tables. Let me also try to look at the FRED (Federal Reserve Economic Data) for this data, as that's the most likely source for this type of information.\n\nActually, I need to find within this document if there's any historical table. Let me look for tables that might contain annual data on saving rates.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_75456dbcf6654e4fadd2d517","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1991_09.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\n# Search for tables with 'after-tax' or 'saving' content\nelements = data['document']['elements']\nfor i, el in enumerate(elements):\n    if el.get('type') == 'table':\n        content = json.dumps(el)\n        if 'saving' in content.lower() or 'after-tax' in content.lower() or 'percent' in content.lower():\n            print(f'Table {i}:')\n            print(content[:2000])\n            print('---')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
